  "profile": {
    "video_id": "kenji:52Gf_0odraY",
    "purpose": "A recipe video showing how to make a homemade version of the McDonald's Big Mac from supermarket ingredients. It covers the onions, the sauce, the bun, the lettuce and smash-style beef patties.",
    "video_type": "how_to",
    "thesis": "You can recreate a Big Mac at home from supermarket ingredients. The key elements are partially dehydrated onions, a mayo-and-mustard sauce (not ketchup), a middle bun cut from a second bottom bun, and beef patties cooked smash-burger style for extra browning.",
    "key_takeaways": [
      "Big Mac onions are dehydrated then rehydrated; at home, finely minced yellow onion microwaved on the lowest power for about 10 minutes approximates them.",
      "Big Mac sauce is mayo and mustard based with pickle relish, not a ketchup-and-mayo Thousand Island style sauce.",
      "The sauce uses mayo, sweet pickle relish, mustard, Marmite for umami, turmeric, sugar, salt and MSG; McDonald's colours theirs with paprika extract.",
      "The middle bun is made by slicing a thin layer off a second bottom bun from cheap, soft supermarket hamburger buns.",
      "Sesame seeds are stuck on with egg white applied by finger, then briefly toasted; a real Big Mac bun has around 600 seeds.",
      "Finely shredded iceberg lettuce soaks up the beef juices.",
      "Patties are just under 2 oz of supermarket 80/20 ground chuck seasoned with salt, pepper and MSG.",
      "The patties are smashed on thick stainless steel (not nonstick or cast iron), cooked about 90% on the first side, then just kissed on the second.",
      "Buns are dry-toasted, and a Big Mac is a 'double single': two patties and one slice of cheese."
    ],
    "outline": [
      {
        "title": "Intro",
        "summary": "Kenji introduces the Big Mac and its components, and says he will recreate it by hand from supermarket ingredients without really changing it.",
        "first_segment": 0,
        "last_segment": 0
      },
      {
        "title": "Making the Sauce",
        "summary": "He starts the onions dehydrating in the microwave, then explains that Big Mac sauce is mayo and mustard based and mixes his version with relish, Dijon, Marmite, turmeric, sugar, salt and MSG.",
        "first_segment": 1,
        "last_segment": 5
      },
      {
        "title": "Making the Bun",
        "summary": "He explains the triple-decker sesame bun, cuts a middle bun from a second bottom bun and applies egg white and sesame seeds before toasting. He also shreds iceberg lettuce.",
        "first_segment": 5,
        "last_segment": 8
      },
      {
        "title": "Cooking the Beef",
        "summary": "He shows the finished microwaved onions, then seasons supermarket ground chuck patties of just under 2 oz and compares them to McDonald's patty sizes and his old Serious Eats recipe.",
        "first_segment": 9,
        "last_segment": 11
      },
      {
        "title": "Smash Burger",
        "summary": "He smashes the patties on the sponsor's Teppanyaki griddle and explains why thick stainless steel gives a better sear. He then dry-toasts the buns and assembles the Big Mac in layers.",
        "first_segment": 11,
        "last_segment": 14
      },
      {
        "title": "Tasting and Recap",
        "summary": "Kenji tastes the burger, shares memories of living above a McDonald's in Harlem, and recaps the key steps of the homemade Big Mac.",
        "first_segment": 15,
        "last_segment": 17
      }
    ],
